    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor; his 80.65 score is head-and-shoulders above the rest of the roster, bolstered by a 0.469 xwOBA against Rocker and a favorable right-handed matchup. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** also emerges as a high-upside play at 69.78, as his elite sprint speed remains our priority in a 5x5 Roto context, and he finds a favorable target in Lodolo despite the platoon disadvantage. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (60.61) captures the final tier of \"Strong\" starts, capitalizing on a significant +11% boost from his platoon advantage against the righty Reynaldo L\u00f3pez, effectively utilizing our roster\u2019s depth to mitigate the difficulty of facing mid-tier arms like Mize and Gilbert.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nelson Velazquez**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 52.37 score. Despite his strong 0.407 xwOBA, the optimizer favored **Chase Meidroth** (52.48) and **Junior Caminero** (53.60) due to their solidified positions in the lineup and more favorable projected output distributions. Furthermore, we must exercise caution with today's rain risks; **Caleb Durbin** (58.31), **Christian Yelich** (53.55), **Pedro Ramirez** (57.97), and **Gary Sanchez** (54.95) all face precipitation threats ranging from 32% to 45%. If the weather impacts these starts, we will look to pivot toward the bench depth provided by **Colt Keith** or **Luke Raley**, though we remain wary of the stiff matchup **Colt Keith** faces against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez, whose 2.84 xERA remains a significant hurdle for any left-handed bat.",
